  "body": "Adds an executable TLA+ model for explicit reaction-state retries. Four writes from an empty state explore 15 states: repeated active writes add evidence at most once, and removal preserves existing addition evidence. The model is included in the social verification runner.\n\nDepends on #360. The refreshed upstream dependency already contains stronger reaction handling, original-time evidence repair and identity redaction; this PR preserves that implementation. Its final diff is model/evidence/documentation, not a replacement handler repair.\n\nTLC passed the 15-state model. The recorded 2,540-example backend run belongs to the earlier candidate before the dependency refresh and is explicitly historical. It does not qualify every behavior of the newer upstream helper. Legacy evidence repair, timestamp collisions and revocation-safe event authorization are outside this model.\n\nNo migration or new runtime behavior. Revert the model/runner addition to roll back this PR; no user data is affected. Keep the dependent social feature gates inactive and the stack unmerged. Draft because broader refinement is incomplete.\n",
